.SH NAME
jags \- Just Another Gibbs Sampler (JAGS)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]jags\f[R] [\f[I]\-d=DEBUGGER\f[R]]
[\f[I]\(endebugger=DEBUGGER\f[R]]
[\f[I]\(endebugger\-args=DEBUGARGS\f[R]] [\f[I]SCRIPTFILE\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]JAGS\f[R] is Just Another Gibbs Sampler.
It is a program for analysis of Bayesian hierarchical models using
Markov Chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) simulation not wholly unlike BUGS.
JAGS was written with three aims in mind:
.IP \(bu 2
To have a cross\-platform engine for the BUGS language
.IP \(bu 2
To be extensible, allowing users to write their own functions,
distributions and samplers
.IP \(bu 2
To be a platform for experimentation with ideas in Bayesian modelling
.PP
This is an official macOS binary of JAGS version VERSIONSTRING compiled
with the following build options:
.IP \(bu 2
BLAS = BLASSTRING
.IP \(bu 2
Multi\-threading = THREADSTRING
.IP \(bu 2
Architecture = ARCHSTRING
.PP
To use other JAGS builds installed on your machine, try the JAGS
utilities jags\-5 and jags\-version.
